{"name":"Asparagus Fern","hex":"#b9cb5a","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"asparagus fern","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Any of several plants in the genus Asparagus which are grown for their ornamental fern-like foliage.\nAsparagus aethiopicus (Sprenger's asparagus), of southern Africa.\nAsparagus densiflorus of southern Africa.\nAsparagus setaceus (syn. Asparagus plumosus, common asparagus fern), of tropical and southern Africa.\nAsparagus virgatus, of tropical and southern Africa.","Asparagus aethiopicus (Sprenger's asparagus), of southern Africa."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/asparagus_fern"}],"entries":[{"title":"Asparagus fern","blocks":[{"text":"Asparagus fern is a common name given to several plants in the genus Asparagus. It may refer to:"},{"items":["Asparagus aethiopicus","Asparagus densiflorus","Asparagus setaceus","Asparagus virgatus"]}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Asparagus_fern","wikidata":"Q4807693"},{"title":"Asparagus","blocks":[{"text":"Asparagus or garden asparagus is a perennial flowering plant species in the genus Asparagus native to Eurasia. Widely cultivated as a vegetable crop, its young shoots are used as a spring vegetable. In 2024, world production of asparagus was 8.9 million tonnes, led by China with 87% of the total."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Asparagus","wikidata":"Q28367"},{"title":"Fern","blocks":[{"text":"Ferns are a group of vascular plants that reproduce via spores and have neither seeds nor flowers. They reproduce in two phases, a short-lived gametophyte that reproduces sexually to develop a spore-bearing leaf structure. Some ferns produce coiled fiddleheads, which expand into fronds."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/47/The_ferns_of_Great_Britain%2C_and_their_allies_the_club-mosses%2C_pepperworts%2C_and_horsetails_%28Pl._2%29_%288515393495%29.jpg/330px-The_ferns_of_Great_Britain%2C_and_their_allies_the_club-mosses%2C_pepperworts%2C_and_horsetails_%28Pl._2%29_%288515393495%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fern","wikidata":"Q80005"},{"title":"Shades of chartreuse","blocks":[{"text":"Shades of chartreuse are listed below. Chartreuse is a color between yellow and green, so named because of its resemblance to the color of the French liqueur green chartreuse."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/17/Shades_of_chartreuse_%28x25%29.svg/330px-Shades_of_chartreuse_%28x25%29.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Shades_of_chartreuse","wikidata":"Q105563495"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3d/Asparagus-Bundle.jpg/500px-Asparagus-Bundle.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3d/Asparagus-Bundle.jpg/1280px-Asparagus-Bundle.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3d/Asparagus-Bundle.jpg/500px-Asparagus-Bundle.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AAsparagus-Bundle.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b0/Asparagus_officinalis_2.jpg/500px-Asparagus_officinalis_2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b0/Asparagus_officinalis_2.jpg/1280px-Asparagus_officinalis_2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b0/Asparagus_officinalis_2.jpg/500px-Asparagus_officinalis_2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Adult plant with fruits","lin